    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's hard to \"wake up\" when everything feels so permanent. like, the machine isn't just the job, it's the whole life. rent, debt, pretending i'm okay just to get through another shift. it's just more fuel for the engine. i look at the clock and i just feel... nothing. just this heavy, empty feeling that there's literally no way out of the cycle.",
